      <p>The following custom resources (CRs) add an <code>example.com/testing</code> label to the <code>unwanted-catalog-1</code> and <code>unwanted-catalog-2</code> cluster catalogs:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"apiVersion: olm.operatorframework.io/v1\nkind: ClusterCatalog\nmetadata:\n  name: unwanted-catalog-1\n  labels:\n    example.com/testing: \"true\"\nspec:\n  source:\n    type: Image\n    image:\n      ref: quay.io/example/content-management-a:latest"} lang="yaml" title="Example cluster catalog CR" />
      <CodeBlock code={"apiVersion: olm.operatorframework.io/v1\nkind: ClusterCatalog\nmetadata:\n  name: unwanted-catalog-2\n  labels:\n    example.com/testing: \"true\"\nspec:\n  source:\n    type: Image\n    image:\n      ref: quay.io/example/content-management-b:latest"} lang="yaml" title="Example cluster catalog CR" />
      <p>The following cluster extension CR excludes selection from the <code>unwanted-catalog-1</code> catalog:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"apiVersion: olm.operatorframework.io/v1\nkind: ClusterExtension\nmetadata:\n  name: <example_extension>\nspec:\n  namespace: <example_namespace>\n  serviceAccount:\n    name: <example_extension>-installer\n  source:\n    sourceType: Catalog\n    catalog:\n      packageName: <example_extension>-operator\n      selector:\n        matchExpressions:\n          - key: olm.operatorframework.io/metadata.name\n            operator: NotIn\n            values:\n              - unwanted-catalog-1"} lang="yaml" title="Example cluster extension CR that excludes a specific catalog" />
      <p>The following cluster extension CR selects from catalogs that do not have the <code>example.com/testing</code> label. As a result, both <code>unwanted-catalog-1</code> and <code>unwanted-catalog-2</code> are excluded from catalog selection.</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"apiVersion: olm.operatorframework.io/v1\nkind: ClusterExtension\nmetadata:\n  name: <example_extension>\nspec:\n  namespace: <example_namespace>\n  serviceAccount:\n    name: <example_extension>-installer\n  source:\n    sourceType: Catalog\n    catalog:\n      packageName: <example_extension>-operator\n      selector:\n        matchExpressions:\n          - key: example.com/testing\n            operator: DoesNotExist"} lang="yaml" title="Example cluster extension CR that excludes catalogs with a specific label" />
      <h2 id="olmv1-catalog-exclusion-by-priority_catalog-content-resolution" class="group scroll-mt-20">Catalog selection by priority<a href="#olmv1-catalog-exclusion-by-priority_catalog-content-resolution" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">When multiple catalogs provide the same package, you can resolve ambiguities by specifying the priority in the custom resource (CR) of each catalog. If unspecified, catalogs have a default priority value of <code>0</code>. The priority can be any positive or negative 32-bit integer.</p>
      <Alert variant="note" class="my-4">
        <AlertTitle>Note</AlertTitle>
        <AlertDescription>
